    {
      "id": "legal_city_zoning_mv",
      "filename": "city_zoning_mv.txt",
      "content": "CITY ZONING AND RENTAL REGULATIONS - MOUNTAIN VIEW, CALIFORNIA\n\nZONING CLASSIFICATIONS:\n- R-3 (Multi-family Residential): Allows up to 4 units per lot\n- R-2 (Two-family Residential): Duplex and accessory dwelling units\n- Mixed-use zones permit ground-floor commercial with residential above\n\nSHORT-TERM RENTAL ORDINANCES:\n- Maximum 90 days per year for unhosted short-term rentals\n- Hosted rentals (owner present) allowed up to 180 days annually\n- Registration required with city planning department\n- Transient occupancy tax (TOT) of 12% applies to all STR income\n- Violations: $500 first offense, $1000 subsequent violations\n\nRENTAL RESTRICTIONS:\n- Rent stabilization ordinance covers properties built before 1995\n- Maximum annual rent increase: 5% or CPI + 5%, whichever is lower\n- Just-cause eviction protections for tenants with 12+ months tenancy\n- Security deposits limited to 2 months rent maximum\n\nPARKING REQUIREMENTS:\n- Minimum 1.5 parking spaces per dwelling unit\n- Electric vehicle charging infrastructure required for new developments\n- Bicycle parking minimum 1 space per unit\n- Guest parking must be clearly marked and accessible\n\nBUILDING CODES:\n- Seismic retrofitting required for buildings constructed before 1980\n- Energy efficiency standards: Title 24 compliance mandatory\n- Fire safety: Sprinkler systems required in buildings over 3 stories\n- Accessibility: ADA compliance required for common areas\n\nPERMIT REQUIREMENTS:\n- Building permits required for structural modifications over $5,000\n- Electrical work over $1,000 requires licensed contractor\n- Plumbing modifications require city inspection\n- Architectural review required for exterior changes in historic districts\n\nPROPERTY TAXES:\n- Base rate: 1.25% of assessed value\n- Additional assessments for infrastructure improvements\n- Senior exemptions available for homeowners 65+ with income under $45,000\n",
