    {
      "id": "legal_hoa_mountain_view",
      "filename": "hoa_mountain_view.txt",
      "content": "HOA RULES AND RESTRICTIONS - MOUNTAIN VIEW, CALIFORNIA\n\nAPPLIANCE RESTRICTIONS:\n- In-unit washer and dryer installations are prohibited in all units\n- Residents must use shared laundry facilities on floors 2 and 4\n- Installation of portable washing machines is strictly forbidden\n- Violations result in $200 fine and immediate removal requirement\n\nPARKING REGULATIONS:\n- Each unit allocated one assigned parking space\n- Guest parking limited to 2 hours maximum\n- No street parking expansion allowed without HOA board approval\n- Electric vehicle charging stations require prior approval and installation fee\n\nSHORT-TERM RENTALS:\n- Airbnb and similar platforms limited to 90 days per calendar year\n- Host must register with HOA and provide proof of insurance\n- No rentals under 30 days without special approval\n- Violations result in $500 fine per incident\n\nNOISE AND OCCUPANCY:\n- Quiet hours enforced 10 PM to 7 AM weekdays, 11 PM to 8 AM weekends\n- Maximum occupancy: 2 persons per bedroom + 1 additional person\n- No commercial activities or home businesses allowed\n\nPROPERTY MODIFICATIONS:\n- Balcony modifications require architectural review committee approval\n- Window treatments must be approved by HOA\n- No satellite dishes or external antennas without approval\n- Landscaping changes require pre-approval\n\nASSESSMENT FEES:\n- Monthly HOA fee: $485 per unit\n- Special assessments may be levied for major repairs\n- Late payment fee: $50 after 15-day grace period\n",
